From u4f3a300f6b3a3a4d at groups.google.com  Wed Oct  2 10:44:00 2013
From: u4f3a300f6b3a3a4d at groups.google.com (borja Varela)
Date: Wed, 02 Oct 2013 10:44:00 +0000
Subject: How to solve the sec-WebSocket-Protocol error in Chrome 30.0.1599.66 m
Message-ID: <hjAHGxBg-6Q.QX4lXHMUDCgJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/hjAHGxBg-6Q/m/QX4lXHMUDCgJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Simply remove the 'shiny' sub-protocol in shini.js in line 453.

Before the change:

      var createSocketFunc = exports.createSocket || function() {
        var ws = new WebSocket('ws://' + window.location.host, 'shiny');
        ws.binaryType = 'arraybuffer';
        return ws;
      };

After the change:

      var createSocketFunc = exports.createSocket || function() {
        var ws = new WebSocket('ws://' + window.location.host);
        ws.binaryType = 'arraybuffer';
        return ws;
      };

It works perfectly for me.

