The Twitter Bootstrap allows for many class styles for buttons.
http://getbootstrap.com/2.3.2/base-css.html#buttons

actionButton <- function(inputId, label, style = "" , additionalClass = "") {
  if (style %in% c("primary","info","success","warning","danger","inverse","link")) {
    class.style <- paste("btn",style,sep="-")
  } else class.style = ""

  tags$button(id=inputId, type="button", class=paste("btn action-button",class.style,additionalClass), label)
}

You can paste the above code after your library(shiny) code to enable more styling for your actionButton.

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-CKGV3UPwYLc/Ul7hzf4fcEI/AAAAAAAADg4/RXtcefTYvto/s1600/actionButton+Styling.png>

https://gist.github.com/xiaodaigh/7012930

shiny::runGist("7012930")

I have done a pull request of the above code. Hopefully it will get incorporate into Shiny proper in the next version

