Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There is a .indexOf() method for JS Arrays, e.g.

x=[0,1,3,9,5]
// [0, 1, 3, 9, 5]
x.indexOf(9)
// 3

If the element is not found, it returns -1.

Regards,
Yihui
--
Yihui Xie <yi...@rstudio.com>
Web: http://yihui.name

