Shiny 0.8 has been great so far, especially thanks to the added direct support of DataTables.  I have successfully played around with most of the options available to DataTables, but I am having trouble with fnCreatedCell.  I found this discussion on the rCharts github <https://github.com/ramnathv/rCharts/issues/192>, but the advice there does not seem to work, I still get the same error:

Uncaught TypeError: Object #! function(nTd, sData, oData, iRow, iCol){ if (sData > 350){ $(nTd).css('color', 'red'); } } !# has no method 'call' jquery.dataTables.min.js:33

Has anyone had any success using functions within DataTables options?

Thanks,
Scott

PS - The example I am trying is trivial, just making a renderDataTable with the mtcars data:

output$datatable <- renderDataTable({ mtcars }, options = list(aoColumnDefs = list(list(
    aTargets = list(2),
    fnCreatedCell = "#! function(nTd, sData, oData, iRow, iCol){
      if (sData > 350){
         $(nTd).css('color', 'red');
      }
    } !#")))
  );

