> As I said, ratioTable() is not reactive to input$sub, but it is called by an output reactive toinput$sub. Is it the cause of the reactivity of the observer ?

No. Reactivity only flows in one direction. Are you sure it's not indirectly reacting to input$sub? You can try the reactlog to visualize the reactive graph.

[Restart R session]
options(shiny.reactlog=TRUE)
runApp()
[Change the "sub" input]
[Press Ctrl+F3]

